course: dictionary
lesson: 13436
title: Horizontal: flat and side to side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Horizontal is a word that tells you which way something lies. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «The shelf is horizontal, so the books will not roll off.» Books stay put only on a flat surface, so horizontal must mean flat and level.
explain: «Draw a horizontal line across the middle of the page.» The word across tells you the line goes from side to side, left to right. Try the swap check: put your meaning in the sentence, "Draw a flat, level line across the middle of the page", and it still makes sense.
explain: In maths, a horizontal line runs along the page like the x-axis. «The spirit level showed the table was horizontal.» A spirit level shows whether something is perfectly level, so horizontal means level and flat. Lines that go up and down are vertical.
fact: Horizontal means flat and level, going straight from side to side.
fact: «Horizontal» is an adjective, so you can say «a horizontal line» or «a horizontal shelf».
fact: In maths, the horizontal axis is the line across the bottom of a graph, going from left to right.
fact: Horizontal is the opposite of vertical, which means straight up and down.
fact: Horizontal lines are parallel to the ground and to the horizon, the line where the sky seems to meet the land.
exercise: «Draw a horizontal line across the middle of the page.» Which way does a horizontal line go? | Diagonally, corner to corner | Round and round in a circle | Up and down, like a tree | *From side to side, left to right
exercise: «The spirit level showed the shelf was horizontal.» What does horizontal mean here? | Standing straight up | *Flat and level | Very heavy | Tilted and sloping
exercise: «The horizontal axis of the graph shows the days of the week.» Which way does the horizontal axis go? | Round in a circle | Up and down | *Along the bottom, from side to side | Into the page
test: What does horizontal mean? | Wobbly and unsteady | Standing straight up | Sloping steeply upwards | *Flat and level, parallel to the ground
test: Which line is horizontal? | A line going down a slide | *A line going straight across from left to right | A line going up a wall | A line that spirals inwards
exam: A horizontal line runs side to side. What does a vertical line do? | Runs round in a circle | Runs side to side | Stays in one spot | *Runs straight up and down
